---
import { SITE_CONFIG } from '../config';
---

<section class="pt-6 pb-12 md:pt-12 md:pb-20">
  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-10 md:gap-16 items-center">
    <div class="max-w-measure">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">Research Engineer at SICK AG · Forward Deployed Engineer</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-[3.25rem] font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50 leading-[1.1] mb-6">
        {SITE_CONFIG.fullname}
      </h1>
      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-4">
        Hey, welcome to my little corner of the internet! Most of my work starts before any code:
        figuring out what someone actually needs.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-4">
        AI has made building cheap. It hasn't made it easier to know what to build. So that is
        where I put my attention: I look at the problem, find out what really matters to the people
        who have it, and build the smallest thing that solves it. Which language or tool that ends
        up being is secondary.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-4">
        Usually the problem is smaller than you'd think. When something becomes possible, it's
        tempting to build everything around it. But most of the time people are annoyed by one
        click too many, or they just want to get data from one spreadsheet into another. I'm not
        out to solve the big problems. I want to make someone's work easier. AI is there to serve
        people, not the other way round.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-8">
        My role keeps evolving with AI.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/blog/" class="btn btn-primary">Read the blog</a>
        <a href="/cv/" class="btn btn-outline">CV</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex justify-start md:justify-end">
      <img
        src="/assets/img/main.jpg"
        alt="Sabine Rümmele"
        class="w-48 h-48 md:w-72 md:h-72 rounded-full object-cover ring-1 ring-brand-200 ring-offset-8 ring-offset-paper dark:ring-brand-900 dark:ring-offset-paper-dark"
        loading="eager"
      />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
